            <ArticleTitle>Coronary spasm in acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>379-84</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a clinical case of coronary spasm in acute myocardial infarction in a 22-year-old patient, admitted to the emergency department with chest pain. Angiography revealed normal coronary arteries and during the procedure a coronary spasm occurred.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
